course: dictionary
lesson: 1061
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job. The word bottle can name an object, name a drink, or name an action. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. In «He drank a bottle of juice», drank tells you the bottle means the drink inside it.
explain: Look for clues. In «A see-saw, scissors, a bottle opener and a wheelbarrow all use levers», the bottle opener is a tool, so bottle is a thing. «Recycle bottles» and «plastic bottle» are things too. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Bottle can also be a verb, a doing word. To bottle something is to put it into bottles. In «Mum will bottle the jam tomorrow», the clue is will, which shows an action in the future. Swap in put into bottles and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A bottle is a container with a narrow neck for holding drinks or other liquids.
fact: «A bottle of» can mean the drink in the container, as in «a bottle of water».
fact: To bottle something means to put it into bottles.
fact: Words like «water bottle» and «bottle cap» are phrases: the first word tells you what kind of bottle it is.
fact: Scientists measure how much a bottle can hold in litres or millilitres.
exercise: «He drank a bottle of juice.» What does bottle mean here? | To put juice into bottles | A bottle opener | *The drink inside the container | A narrow neck
exercise: «Mum will bottle the jam tomorrow.» What does bottle mean here? | A drink for breakfast | *To put into bottles | A tool for opening caps | A small glass container
exercise: In «a water bottle», what does bottle name? | The sound it makes | A kind of water | To fill something up | *A container for liquids
test: Scientists measure the capacity of a bottle in what units? | Kilograms | *Litres or millilitres | Seconds | Metres
test: «Water is strange: it grows bigger when it freezes, which is why a full bottle cracks in the freezer.» Why does the bottle crack? | The bottle is empty | *Water grows bigger when it freezes | The bottle was left in the sun | Its glass is too thin for any liquid
exam: Which sentence uses bottle as a verb? | The bottle cap is red. | He bought a plastic bottle. | *Please bottle the juice before lunch. | She holds a water bottle.
